{
  "abstract": "We construct a counterexample to the generalized Nandakumar--Ramana Rao problem: in every dimension d > 17, there are d − 1 continuous functionals on convex bodies and a probability measure such that there is no convex partition of the unit ball into six parts of equal measure on which all these functionals are equalized. We also show that the topological Tverberg conjecture fails for sixfold intersections already in ℝ⁶: we construct a continuous map Δ³⁵ → ℝ⁶ whose images of six pairwise disjoint faces never meet.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Arseniy Akopyan"
    }
  ],
